From: qineng-det <det@topogym.local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:00:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] cuda: reproducible FastSegmentalReduce (TopoGym
 determinism series 3/4)

FastSegmentalReduce (matrix converter: duplicate triplet blocks and doublet
segments; external articulation constraint: G^theta) reduces every warp's
piece of a segment with cub's warp-segmented reduce, then atomically added
the pieces of a segment that crosses a warp boundary into out(key): with
three or more pieces the order followed the scheduler.

Atomics replaced:
- fast_segmental_reduce.inl (scalar and matrix variants): pass 1 takes
  the head flags straight from the keys, reduces every piece in the warp's
  fixed shuffle order and lets the piece's head assign out(key); pass 2
  (one thread per segment start) overwrites every segment that crosses a
  warp boundary with the in-order reduction of all its elements.

Pass 1 no longer reads cub's reduced flags word: the invalid lanes of
the last, partly filled warp (key -1, neighbour keys not read, also -1)
join the input's last segment, and lane 31 among them flags it as
cross-warp. Upstream tolerated that (an atomic add into the zero-filled
output); a write rule keyed on the flag drops the segment (the first
version of this patch did: preconditioner NaN at rope_threading medium
frame 121).
